<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Qi forge (plan de fusion, 2026-10-23): the qi version of the machining table. It tempers any weapon, qi or mortal, one
    spirit grade at a time (+1 quality level each time), and makes the qi cannons that turn any turret into a qi turret.
    Each temper recipe accepts only weapons of one grade, so the price grows with the grade and there is no fixed cap.
    Balance (user: be generous): the forge and cannon I come early, right after the Convergence.
    Art by the user: Things/Building/CVG/QiTech/QiForge, Things/Item/CVG/QiTech/QiCannon_I..III.
  -->

  <ResearchProjectDef>
    <defName>CVG_Research_QiForging</defName>
    <tab>CVG_SpiritualEngineering</tab>
    <label>qi forging</label>
    <description>The first thing the smiths of the Rim learned after the Convergence was that a spirit stone in the quench water changes the steel. Qi forging turns that accident into a method: an electric forge that tempers weapons with qi, one grade at a time, and casts the qi cannons that let any turret wound a cultivator. Unlocks the qi forge, the first temperings and the qi cannon I. The sects learned the same art in a thousand years; the smiths of the Rim learned it in one bad winter.</description>
    <baseCost>800</baseCost>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <prerequisites>
      <li>Smithing</li>
      <li>Electricity</li>
    </prerequisites>
    <researchViewX>0</researchViewX>
    <researchViewY>5</researchViewY>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="Convergence.QiTech.DefModExtension_RequiresConvergence" />
    </modExtensions>
  </ResearchProjectDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BenchBase">
    <defName>CVG_QiForge</defName>
    <label>qi forge</label>
    <description>An electric forge of black iron and brass around a quench basin fed with dissolved spirit stone. It tempers weapons with qi: each tempering raises the spirit grade by one and the quality by one level, so a weapon that only scratched a cultivator learns to wound them. It also casts the qi cannons for turrets and the qi cores for mechanoids. The Heavenly Cauldron Pavilion calls it a crude copy of a sect furnace and keeps three of them in its own workshops.</description>
    <thingClass>Building_WorkTable</thingClass>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/CVG/QiTech/QiForge</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(3.5,2.25)</drawSize>
      <damageData>
        <cornerTL>Damage/Corner</cornerTL>
        <cornerTR>Damage/Corner</cornerTR>
        <cornerBL>Damage/Corner</cornerBL>
        <cornerBR>Damage/Corner</cornerBR>
      </damageData>
    </graphicData>
    <castEdgeShadows>true</castEdgeShadows>
    <staticSunShadowHeight>0.20</staticSunShadowHeight>
    <costList>
      <Steel>150</Steel>
      <ComponentIndustrial>4</ComponentIndustrial>
      <CVG_SpiritStone>20</CVG_SpiritStone>
    </costList>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <fillPercent>0.5</fillPercent>
    <useHitPoints>True</useHitPoints>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>40</Mass>
      <WorkToBuild>4000</WorkToBuild>
      <MaxHitPoints>220</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <Cleanliness>-2</Cleanliness>
    </statBases>
    <size>(3,2)</size>
    <designationCategory>CVG_QiTech</designationCategory>
    <passability>PassThroughOnly</passability>
    <pathCost>50</pathCost>
    <hasInteractionCell>True</hasInteractionCell>
    <interactionCellOffset>(0,0,-1)</interactionCellOffset>
    <surfaceType>Item</surfaceType>
    <constructionSkillPrerequisite>4</constructionSkillPrerequisite>
    <inspectorTabs>
      <li>ITab_Bills</li>
    </inspectorTabs>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_ReportWorkSpeed">
        <workSpeedStat>WorkTableWorkSpeedFactor</workSpeedStat>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Power">
        <compClass>CompPowerTrader</compClass>
        <shortCircuitInRain>true</shortCircuitInRain>
        <basePowerConsumption>250</basePowerConsumption>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Flickable" />
      <li Class="CompProperties_Glower">
        <glowRadius>5</glowRadius>
        <glowColor>(80,220,210,0)</glowColor>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_AffectedByFacilities">
        <linkableFacilities>
          <li>ToolCabinet</li>
        </linkableFacilities>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Breakdownable" />
    </comps>
    <building>
      <buildingTags>
        <li>Production</li>
      </buildingTags>
      <spawnedConceptLearnOpportunity>BillsTab</spawnedConceptLearnOpportunity>
      <workTableRoomRole>Workshop</workTableRoomRole>
      <workTableNotInRoomRoleFactor>0.8</workTableNotInRoomRoleFactor>
    </building>
    <constructEffect>ConstructMetal</constructEffect>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>CVG_Research_QiForging</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <placeWorkers>
      <li>PlaceWorker_ReportWorkSpeedPenalties</li>
      <li>PlaceWorker_ShowFacilitiesConnections</li>
      <li>PlaceWorker_PreventInteractionSpotOverlap</li>
    </placeWorkers>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="Convergence.DefModExtension_Forge" />
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

